  <p class="blog-lede" slot="lede">
    Mainland summer mega-sales are rarely a single midnight—they are <strong>multi-wave inventories</strong> with parallel presale mechanics.
    On <strong>29 April 2026</strong>, Sina Tech republished Tmall&apos;s merchant-facing briefing stating that <strong>618 opens 21 May</strong> with <strong>presale running alongside spot inventory</strong>.
    Kakobuy Spreadsheet shoppers should translate those headlines into warehouse realism: agents ingest parcels as domestic carriers scan them, not when influencer countdown timers hit zero.
  </p>

  <h2>What the April 2026 briefing actually spells out</h2>
  <p>
    According to the article on <a href="https://finance.sina.com.cn/tech/roll/2026-04-29/doc-inhwefve6787805.shtml" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">finance.sina.com.cn</a> (29 April 2026, citing Tmall merchant rules):
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Presale segment:</strong> 21 May → 3 June.</li>
    <li><strong>Spot “rush buy” wave:</strong> 21–30 May.</li>
    <li><strong>Second carnival wave:</strong> 31 May → 21 June.</li>
    <li><strong>Fulfilment SLA emphasis:</strong> for fee-paid Tmall promo orders, merchants must ship within <strong>48 hours</strong>, produce a pickup scan, and refresh logistics within <strong>24 hours</strong> of pickup—still plenty of room for carrier chokepoints reflected in our <a href="/blog/china-public-holidays-agent-forwarding-2026/">2026 holiday logistics essay</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Platforms iterate micro-rules after publication—always reconcile against the merchant PDF you receive inside seller consoles—but spreadsheets should cite <strong>capture dates</strong> when quoting waves so readers know whether advice is stale.
  </p>

  <h2>Spreadsheet behaviours that survive the promo fog</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Wave-tag rows:</strong> mark whether a SKU was presale deposit vs spot cart—mixing them in one consolidated Kakobuy outbound parcel invites timing skew.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Domestic tracking cadence:</strong> silence during mega-sales often reflects mesh backlog, not fraud—pair expectations with <a href="/blog/kakobuy-spreadsheet-to-parcel-checklist/">parcel checklist discipline</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Warehouse storage coupling:</strong> when arrivals trickle across weeks, storage clocks still advance—see <a href="/blog/kakobuy-warehouse-storage-spreadsheet/">warehouse storage primer</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Scope honesty</h2>
  <p>
    This article summarises <strong>Chinese-language trade press</strong>, not Kakobuy-internal throughput dashboards.
    Binding fulfilment quotes remain inside Kakobuy after items reach their warehouse; festival hype merely explains why domestic legs stop behaving like ordinary Tuesdays.
  </p>
